[
    {
        "content": "<p>I met with this problem when making a tactic for Hoare triple (see <a href=\"https://softwarefoundations.cis.upenn.edu\">SF</a>). Here's a simplified version:</p>\n<p>An <em>assertion</em> (on <code>Nat</code>) is a function of type <code>Nat → Prop</code> and a <em>triple</em> consists of two assertions <code>P, Q</code> and a function <code>f: Nat → Nat</code> such that <code>forall m, P m → Q (f m)</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Assertion</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Triple</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Assertion</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Assertion</span><span class=\"o\">):</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">forall</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>We say <code>P: Assertion</code> <em>implies</em> <code>Q: Assertion</code> if <code>P n</code> implies<code>Q n</code> forall <code>n: Nat</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Assertion</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">implies</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Assertion</span><span class=\"o\">):</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">forall</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Naively, we have the following theorem helping us change the post-assertion.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Triple</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">post</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q'</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Assertion</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">}:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q'</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">implies</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">Triple</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">Triple</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span>\n<span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">intros</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Triple</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Assertion</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">implies</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>In the case of Hoare triple, this can help us to change the goal to the <em>loop invariant</em>.</p>\n<p>For example, we can define the following assertions and prove <code>le3</code> implies <code>le4</code></p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">):</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le2</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Assertion</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le3</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Assertion</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le4</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Assertion</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">4</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le3_implies_le4</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le3</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">implies</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le4</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">le3</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le4</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Assertion</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">implies</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>One example usage of <code>Triple.post</code> is the following.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Triple</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le4</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">apply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Triple</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">post</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Q'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le3</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le3_implies_le4</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- the goal is turned to `Triple le2 inc le3`</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">inc</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le2</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le3</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Since I need to change the post-assertion frequently, I made the following tactic.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">macro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"change_post\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q'</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\":=\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"n\">apply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Triple</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">post</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Q'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">Q'</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>It worked well:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Triple</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le4</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">change_post</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le3_implies_le4</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">inc</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le2</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le3</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>However, if it failed when I tried to use <code>by</code> instead of <code>le3_implies_le4</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Triple</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le4</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">change_post</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">apply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le3_implies_le4</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">inc</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le2</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le3</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>It seems that in this case, Lean failed to unify terms with <code>Triple</code>. I further did the following experiments:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Triple</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le4</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">apply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Triple</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">post</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le3_implies_le4</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">inc</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le2</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le3</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Using <code>Triple.post</code> without any argument worked just fine, and in this case, only <code>Q'</code> was unknown. However, if you only specify <code>Q'</code>, it still fails.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Triple</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le4</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">apply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Triple</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">post</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Q'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le3</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le3_implies_le4</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">inc</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le2</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le3</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>But if you specify both <code>Q</code> and <code>Q'</code>, it works again.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Triple</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le4</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">apply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Triple</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">post</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le4</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Q'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le3</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le3_implies_le4</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">inc</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le2</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le3</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>And I checked the types, which looked good.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Triple</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">post</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Q'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le3</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- Triple.post : le3.implies ?m.2 → Triple ?m.1 ?m.3 le3 → Triple ?m.1 ?m.3 ?m.2</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Triple</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">post</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Q'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le3</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le4</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- Triple.post : le3.implies le4 → Triple ?m.1 ?m.2 le3 → Triple ?m.1 ?m.2 le4</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Interestingly, the change of <code>pre-assertion</code> works well.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Triple</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">pre</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Assertion</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">}:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">implies</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P'</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">Triple</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">Triple</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span>\n<span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">intros</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Triple</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Assertion</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">implies</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n\n<span class=\"kn\">macro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"change_pre\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P'</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\":=\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"n\">apply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">@</span><span class=\"n\">Triple</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">pre</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">P'</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Triple</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le4</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">change_pre</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Triple</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le2</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le3</span><span class=\"o\">])</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">inc</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le3</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le4</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Note that I used <code>@Triple.pre</code> instead of <code>Triple.pre</code>. The latter also made lean complain about unification problems.</p>\n<p>Full code can be found <a href=\"https://live.lean-lang.org/#codez=CYUwZgBAggzjICcAuBLA9gOwgLgLwQDkBDJCQJMIIAFBNABwCh7RIAVBFWgGxAgApLs0OIlSYAlHwDGg4qQqyJvAIqDY8ZOgxjB1Ojlz0IEMGgRFOnCAFsANFWvkISqdbGMm4IetEYAdCisuFBAYPkonVWENcR0aWn1DY1NzSww7cKwKZwx3JAALEFMQKwg2Dm5fWjQYUgBvcOclAHJI700AXwha6UISR1l27ETeAElBZv9AzmDQpQkyRLKuHnDJJybyRfZl%2BzWlejwIACMAT0SUDCQaGESAc3YMYAgAbSXuOzURTUmgkIBddzMCAXNa8AAeMhI2l6pEOYIgAGoIABGDyQbgAJlaX0w%2BmMAFcsPDcAA%2BCDwwAmRBAMWiINwAMzY6JYQ5gQnkiCkjlU%2Bm07gAFiZPjxbKJnLJlIg%2FNyBSKJQZAH0Ar8YAqBYIGT9piE6SB%2BXjTncHk9ngy7AKPlEfFqZgDGCAwUQpiBBG8eJjgRg1gKDWcjERaFwTqVthUqjU%2BM08QyJIrldrVQLEgBaZMQfI8W5oczA0JIfEIDAgJ5INAQAAGbt1GM93pA9PL50uNAgCtbRouJpB5pAGJ79Lt9CsREkLYARJI8kQMLcQArw0gx%2BtsEhECUx3gl0gV2ucOmR6g1qTEuXeEgDyhJAAfANBkPlECVaqkZQbQ4AEmaihGePfSDEbj2o6zquqG7q9rWur6ochpGJO06zvOz66vS0b1kqUwzGqepNlcZZtgqHaPC83bVv2g4Ok6yygQ%2B1aQT6MF%2BhA8EznOC4ob6EC3pwwZxphITYdKRgXHhrbtkY9ydiRXo9n2KEUcB1H3jsHoglBvqJNxwZuk%2BNSJL4ECUZIpB8Sqgn6Z6okEYkEnGtJkiyeR7iUSByncHRakMfgsFcYGPFuY%2B7Gvmh9JuEYBlGSZ6HxlhSbhZZLbWUYtlSc8pGYk5QFUdwNEqRBnl6hp%2Fp%2BdpYG6S%2BziHAKihRlV9ZhRAEWOsZKEYWZcUJfh4kQJJxFpTJZHye4ADEk4gJIADWAXlZGb74DGRiptN7EavWNo6gA%2FFYvg1hQVZbb4yIQAdqEMo4%2B3bUdJ3HdtNKjQUk3LchwV1aFkZofyEhLTpK0oetoQ%2BntYE3YdIM1mdQO0QdV23VBMqFAgxTLYjXThJQGwqF4OIYJ03SQnIMKDMMYxUP9VBNPMWy0ejzFOJsRhVqsTgHN5TEidcREmm6lptJg%2F2DsOo5lhOU6sfOiNLujO4IOum7ptLJSCOexmXuKJ5nhe15aRAAACP0o%2Fwc0QO%2B6Pfr%2B%2F6AfQLlKVWqleupjGJCxiG0CjZ2MXw7NdQqADcPV2a8YGOfJDVe2JhEpX16X1j2%2FIAkAA\">here</a>.</p>\n<p>Lean said it could not unify <code>?m.3 (?m.4 ?m)</code> with the goal <code>Triple le2 inc le4</code>. It seems that <code>?m.3 (?m.4 ?m)</code> is derived from <code>forall m, P m → Q (c m)</code> as in the definition of <code>Triple</code>. Does this mean that Lean has done too much unfolding  or did I miss something?</p>",
        "id": 622738876,
