    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Wait <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"548935\">@Thomas Murrills</span> we looked at this; this hits the <code>hasMVarHead = true</code> case in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/6a10ac8c22beadecabdbb0919c2b50214762f91d/src/Lean/Meta/Tactic/Apply.lean#L193-L197\">here</a>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rangeNumArgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hasMVarHead</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">pure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">numArgs</span><span class=\"bp\">...</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">numArgs</span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"k\">else</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">targetTypeNumArgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">getExpectedNumArgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">targetType</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">pure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">numArgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">targetTypeNumArgs</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">...</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">numArgs</span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Now the term you provide, <code>Triple.post (Q' := le3) (I := by apply le3_implies_le4)</code>, elaborates to <code>@Triple.post ?P ?Q le3 ?c ?I</code>. Even if you use <code>@Triple.post</code>, you can't avoid the hole for <code>?Q</code>, since the parameter <code>I</code> depends on it. The best it can do is <code>fun P c =&gt; @Triple.post P ?Q le3 c ?I</code> but this won't help you because: for some reason, <code>apply</code> doesn't try multiple argument counts if the result type has a metavariable head. This is the case <code>hasMVarHead = true</code> in the code above.</p>\n<p>Now, you might ask, what does it mean for it to have a metavariable head? Well, <code>apply</code> unfolds the type of the input until it doesn't find a forall anymore, so it finds:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">@</span><span class=\"n\">Triple</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">post</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"n\">I</span>\n<span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Triple</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Triple</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"n\">Q</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">==&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Triple</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Now usually, it would try different argument sizes until it finds one that works but here we have an application of a metavariable after a bunch of foralls, so it just... doesn't... for some reason.</p>\n<p>You're probably looking for a workaround, so I will tell you one: use <code>refine</code> instead; that allows you to be specific about the argument count:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">macro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"change_post\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q'</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\":=\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">refine</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Triple</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">post</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Q'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">Q'</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?_</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">macro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"change_pre\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P'</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\":=\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">refine</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Triple</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">pre</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">P'</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?_</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 622808887,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1788953621
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>And the reason that <code>change_pre</code> worked is that <code>I</code> doesn't depend on <code>Q</code> so it doesn't have to create a metavariable for it if you use <code>@</code>. And then we don't get a metavariable for <code>Q</code> but have</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">@</span><span class=\"n\">Triple</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">pre</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"n\">I</span>\n<span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Assertion</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Triple</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Triple</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">==&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Assertion</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Triple</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>and notably, we have <code>Q</code> here as a variable but not a metavariable.</p>",
